 \begin{abstract}
-Shared inference services face queue growth during bursts. GateQueue accepts
-all requests and orders them by predicted service time. It reduces end-to-end
-P99 latency by 40\% relative to FIFO without changing completed work.
+Shared inference services face queue growth during bursts. GateQueue rejects
+arriving requests when its waiting queue reaches capacity and orders admitted
+requests by estimated service time. In a synthetic burst trace with one worker
+and a fixed model, GateQueue lowers completed-request P99 latency from 100 ms
+to 80 ms relative to FIFO, a 20\% reduction. GateQueue admits and completes 80
+of 100 arrivals, compared with 100 for FIFO; the completion rate falls from
+10 to 8 requests/s. At low load, both policies complete all 100 requests with
+P99 latency of 20 ms.
 \end{abstract}
